- # `↯/s.34.1` — `Regex.Error`
+ # `↯/s.34.1` — `Regex.Error`

- Raised when Kaleidoscope cannot parse a regular expression literal.
- Each variant pinpoints the syntactic problem.
+ Sollevato quando Kaleidoscope non riesce ad analizzare un letterale di espressione regolare.
+ Ogni variante individua con precisione il problema sintattico.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- The `r"…"` regex interpolator parses the pattern at compile time. When
- the parser cannot accept the input, it throws a `Regex.Error` carrying
- the character `index` at which the problem was detected and a `Reason`
- explaining what was expected. The constructed message is `the regular
- expression could not be parsed because $reason at $index`.
+ L'interpolatore regex `r"…"` analizza il pattern in fase di compilazione. Quando il parser non può
+ accettare l'input, lancia un `Regex.Error` che porta l'`index` del carattere in cui il problema è
+ stato rilevato e un `Reason` che spiega che cosa ci si aspettava. Il messaggio costruito è
+ `the regular expression could not be parsed because $reason at $index`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Varianti

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.34.1.1`  `UnclosedGroup`  A capturing group was opened with `(` but never closed with `)`.  `[↯/s.34.1.1] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was not closed at 11`  Add the missing `)` or escape the `(` if a literal parenthesis is intended.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.2`  `ExpectedGroup`  An extractor pattern was used in a context that requires a capturing group to follow it, but no group was found.  `[↯/s.34.1.2] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was expected immediately following an extractor at 0`  Wrap the extracted portion of the pattern in `(…)`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.3`  `BadRepetition`  A repetition range `{n,m}` has `m < n`.  `[↯/s.34.1.3] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions is less than the minimum at 5`  Swap the bounds, or use `{n,}` if no upper bound is needed.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.4`  `Uncapturable`  A capturing group is nested inside a repeating group, which means it cannot be extracted unambiguously.  `[↯/s.34.1.4] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group inside a repeating group can not be extracted at 7`  Either remove the capture by switching to a non-capturing group `(?:…)`, or restructure the pattern so the repetition is inside the capture rather than outside it.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.5`  `UnexpectedChar`  A character that does not belong in a repetition range was encountered.  `[↯/s.34.1.5] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range contained an unexpected character at 9`  Use only digits and a single comma between `{` and `}`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.6`  `NotInGroup`  A `)` was encountered with no corresponding `(`.  `[↯/s.34.1.6] the regular expression could not be parsed because a closing parenthesis was found without a corresponding opening parenthesis at 4`  Add the missing `(`, escape the `)` if it should be literal, or remove the stray closing parenthesis.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.7`  `IncompleteRepetition`  A repetition range was opened with `{` but never closed with `}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.7] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range was not closed at 8`  Add the missing `}`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.8`  `InvalidPattern`  The pattern was rejected by the underlying parser for a reason that does not fit any of the more specific variants.  `[↯/s.34.1.8] the regular expression could not be parsed because the pattern was invalid at 3`  Review the pattern around the reported index; consult the regex syntax for the construct in use.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.9`  `UnclosedEscape`  The pattern ends with a `\` that has nothing to escape.  `` [↯/s.34.1.9] the regular expression could not be parsed because nothing followed the escape character `\` at 12 ``  Either remove the trailing backslash or escape the character that should follow it.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.10`  `EmptyCharClass`  A character class `[…]` contained no characters.  `[↯/s.34.1.10] the regular expression could not be parsed because the character class is empty at 2`  Add at least one character to the class, or remove the empty `[]`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.11`  `ZeroMaximum`  A repetition range had a maximum of zero, e.g. `{0,0}` or `{0}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.11] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions must be greater than zero at 6`  Use a maximum greater than zero, or remove the repeated subpattern entirely if it should never match.
+ column  Codice
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significato
+ column  Messaggio
+ column  Soluzione
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.1`  `UnclosedGroup`  Un gruppo di cattura è stato aperto con `(` ma mai chiuso con `)`.  `[↯/s.34.1.1] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was not closed at 11`  Aggiungere la `)` mancante o fare l'escape della `(` se si intende una parentesi letterale.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.2`  `ExpectedGroup`  Un pattern estrattore è stato usato in un contesto che richiede che sia seguito da un gruppo di cattura, ma non è stato trovato alcun gruppo.  `[↯/s.34.1.2] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was expected immediately following an extractor at 0`  Racchiudere la porzione estratta del pattern in `(…)`.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.3`  `BadRepetition`  Un intervallo di ripetizione `{n,m}` ha `m < n`.  `[↯/s.34.1.3] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions is less than the minimum at 5`  Scambiare i limiti, o usare `{n,}` se non serve un limite superiore.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.4`  `Uncapturable`  Un gruppo di cattura è annidato in un gruppo che si ripete, il che significa che non può essere estratto senza ambiguità.  `[↯/s.34.1.4] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group inside a repeating group can not be extracted at 7`  Rimuovere la cattura passando a un gruppo non di cattura `(?:…)`, oppure ristrutturare il pattern in modo che la ripetizione sia dentro la cattura anziché fuori.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.5`  `UnexpectedChar`  È stato incontrato un carattere che non appartiene a un intervallo di ripetizione.  `[↯/s.34.1.5] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range contained an unexpected character at 9`  Usare solo cifre e una sola virgola tra `{` e `}`.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.6`  `NotInGroup`  È stata incontrata una `)` senza una `(` corrispondente.  `[↯/s.34.1.6] the regular expression could not be parsed because a closing parenthesis was found without a corresponding opening parenthesis at 4`  Aggiungere la `(` mancante, fare l'escape della `)` se deve essere letterale, o rimuovere la parentesi di chiusura spaiata.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.7`  `IncompleteRepetition`  Un intervallo di ripetizione è stato aperto con `{` ma mai chiuso con `}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.7] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range was not closed at 8`  Aggiungere la `}` mancante.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.8`  `InvalidPattern`  Il pattern è stato rifiutato dal parser sottostante per un motivo che non rientra in nessuna delle varianti più specifiche.  `[↯/s.34.1.8] the regular expression could not be parsed because the pattern was invalid at 3`  Rivedere il pattern attorno all'indice riportato; consultare la sintassi regex per il costrutto in uso.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.9`  `UnclosedEscape`  Il pattern termina con un `\` che non ha nulla di cui fare l'escape.  `` [↯/s.34.1.9] the regular expression could not be parsed because nothing followed the escape character `\` at 12 ``  Rimuovere la barra rovesciata finale o fare l'escape del carattere che dovrebbe seguirla.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.10`  `EmptyCharClass`  Una classe di caratteri `[…]` non conteneva alcun carattere.  `[↯/s.34.1.10] the regular expression could not be parsed because the character class is empty at 2`  Aggiungere almeno un carattere alla classe, o rimuovere la `[]` vuota.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.11`  `ZeroMaximum`  Un intervallo di ripetizione aveva un massimo pari a zero, ad esempio `{0,0}` o `{0}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.11] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions must be greater than zero at 6`  Usare un massimo maggiore di zero, o rimuovere del tutto il sottopattern ripetuto se non deve mai trovare corrispondenze.

